NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000308 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000309 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000310 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000311 "Sub::Install - install subroutines into packages easily"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000312 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000313 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000314 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000315 "version 0.929"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000316 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000317 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000318 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000319 "  use Sub::Install;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000320 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000321 "  Sub::Install::install_sub({"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000322 "    code => sub { ... },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000323 "    into => $package,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000324 "    as   => $subname"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000325 "  });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000326 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000327 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 "This module makes it easy to install subroutines into packages without the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 "unsightly mess of C<no strict> or typeglobs lying about where just anyone can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 "see them."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 "=head1 PERL VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 "This library should run on perls released even an extremely long time ago.  It"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 "should work on any version of perl released in the last ten years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 "Although it may work on older versions of perl, no guarantee is made that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 "minimum required version will not be increased.  The version may be increased"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 "for any reason, and there is no promise that patches will be accepted to lower"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 "the minimum required perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 "=head2 install_sub"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 "  Sub::Install::install_sub({"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 "   code => \\&subroutine,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 "   into => \"Finance::Shady\","
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 "   as   => 'launder',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "  });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "This routine installs a given code reference into a package as a normal"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 "subroutine.  The above is equivalent to:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "  no strict 'refs';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "  *{\"Finance::Shady\" . '::' . \"launder\"} = \\&subroutine;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "If C<into> is not given, the sub is installed into the calling package."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 "If C<code> is not a code reference, it is looked for as an existing sub in the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 "package named in the C<from> parameter.  If C<from> is not given, it will look"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 "in the calling package."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 "If C<as> is not given, and if C<code> is a name, C<as> will default to C<code>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 "If C<as> is not given, but if C<code> is a code ref, Sub::Install will try to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 "find the name of the given code ref and use that as C<as>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 "That means that this code:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 "  Sub::Install::install_sub({"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 "    code => 'twitch',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "    from => 'Person::InPain',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 "    into => 'Person::Teenager',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 "    as   => 'dance',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "  });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 "is the same as:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 "  package Person::Teenager;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 "  Sub::Install::install_sub({"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 "    code => Person::InPain->can('twitch'),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 "    as   => 'dance',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 "  });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "=head2 reinstall_sub"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 "This routine behaves exactly like C<L</install_sub>>, but does not emit a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 "warning if warnings are on and the destination is already defined."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "=head2 install_installers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 "This routine is provided to allow Sub::Install compatibility with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 "Sub::Installer.  It installs C<install_sub> and C<reinstall_sub> methods into"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 "the package named by its argument."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 " Sub::Install::install_installers('Code::Builder'); # just for us, please"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 " Code::Builder->install_sub({ name => $code_ref });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 " Sub::Install::install_installers('UNIVERSAL'); # feeling lucky, punk?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 " Anything::At::All->install_sub({ name => $code_ref });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "The installed installers are similar, but not identical, to those provided by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 "Sub::Installer.  They accept a single hash as an argument.  The key/value pairs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "are used as the C<as> and C<code> parameters to the C<install_sub> routine"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 "detailed above.  The package name on which the method is called is used as the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 "C<into> parameter."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "Unlike Sub::Installer's C<install_sub> will not eval strings into code, but"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 "will look for named code in the calling package."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 "=head1 EXPORTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 "Sub::Install exports C<install_sub> and C<reinstall_sub> only if they are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "requested."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 "=head2 exporter"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "Sub::Install has a never-exported subroutine called C<exporter>, which is used"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "to implement its C<import> routine.  It takes a hashref of named arguments,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "only one of which is currently recognize: C<exports>.  This must be an arrayref"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "of subroutines to offer for export."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 "This routine is mainly for Sub::Install's own consumption.  Instead, consider"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "L<Sub::Exporter>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "=item L<Sub::Installer>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 "This module is (obviously) a reaction to Damian Conway's Sub::Installer, which"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 "does the same thing, but does it by getting its greasy fingers all over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "UNIVERSAL.  I was really happy about the idea of making the installation of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 "coderefs less ugly, but I couldn't bring myself to replace the ugliness of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "typeglobs and loosened strictures with the ugliness of UNIVERSAL methods."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "=item L<Sub::Exporter>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 "This is a complete Exporter.pm replacement, built atop Sub::Install."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 "=head1 EXTRA CREDITS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 "Several of the tests are adapted from tests that shipped with Damian Conway's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "Sub-Installer distribution."
